From cc86ed5e93dcf961fc7a03fbe29a915878801038 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitry B <dimitryB@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:53:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] eip155: report a replayed authorization as
 invalid_transaction_state
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Settling (or verifying) an EIP-3009 authorization or Permit2 permit whose nonce
was already used makes the transfer simulation or gas estimate revert
("FiatTokenV2: authorization is used or canceled", Permit2 InvalidNonce()).
That revert surfaced as a transport error: HTTP 500 with unexpected_error.

When the transfer fails to execute, read the authorization state on chain
(EIP-3009 authorizationState, Permit2 nonceBitmap). If the nonce is spent,
report PaymentVerificationError::AuthorizationAlreadyUsed, which maps to the
x402 v2 §9 code invalid_transaction_state ("Blockchain transaction failed or
was rejected"): the chain rejects the transfer because of on-chain state. §9
has no replay-specific code; invalid_payload would wrongly call a once-valid
payload malformed, and unexpected_*_error would invite retries that cannot
succeed. The state is read only after a failure, so successful payments make
no extra RPC call. Failures after broadcast (receipt timeouts) are not
reclassified.
